Subject: [Wine 11.0] Fold legacy HLSL pow before lowering to logarithms.

Local fix, not an upstream backport.

3DMark06 HDR Canyon Flight computes 1 / pow(1 - 1.12, 2) and similar
expressions. Lowering pow to exp2(exponent * log2(base)) at parse time
turns their negative bases into invalid logarithms during constant folding.
Microsoft D3DX28 and D3DX43 accept these finite power expressions but reject
explicit negative log2 constants. Preserve that distinction by retaining a
POW expression until folding, then lower remaining nonconstant expressions
to the previous instruction sequence. Apply this only to shader models 1-3;
the SM4+ path and logarithm validation are unchanged.

Regression: tools/buildWine/probes/hlsl-legacy-pow.c verifies constant
results as well as rejection of undefined expressions. Repeat both 3DMark06
HDR/SM3.0 scenes when changing this patch.

